Read and follow the GSD workflow file at $HOME/.codex/gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase.md for phase 47 --auto. The `--auto` flag is part of the workflow invocation and must be preserved verbatim.

## Advisory incremental self-review

After each plan or wave lands, perform a quick, shallow self-check for doc accuracy, leaked data, CI/build correctness, and external-state claims. Record any drift in the working output and continue execution; this self-check is not the authoritative review of the phase. This check must not pause execution or request human input.

## Operator-only checkpoints

A package-verification checkpoint and a blocking-human gate are the operator's: ask through devflow_ask and apply the answer you receive. If the devflow_ask call itself fails, do not self-resolve or approve one under any circumstances, and report it instead. When devflow_ask fails and you report a blocking-human gate that you or a subagent you ran stopped at, say so on your final line with the checkpoint field, for example `DEVFLOW_RESULT: {"status": "failed", "checkpoint": "blocking-human", "reason": "which gate stopped and the decision it needs"}`. Use the checkpoint field for nothing else: not for a gate the operator answered, and not for any other failure.

## Questions go to the operator

When you reach a decision checkpoint, a `blocking-human` gate, a package-verification checkpoint, or a question a GSD workflow would ask the user (including a discuss question), call the `devflow_ask` tool from the `devflow` MCP server. Clients namespace it: Claude Code lists it as `mcp__devflow__devflow_ask`, and codex as tool `devflow_ask` of server `devflow`; call the name your tool list shows for that server's `devflow_ask`. Pass the question, every option as `{id, label, description}`, the context the operator needs, `kind` (`decision`, `blocking-human` or `discuss`), and `recommended` if one option is recommended. Wait for the answer and apply exactly that answer. Do not choose an option yourself, do not choose by position, and do not stop with a report instead of asking. When a GSD subagent you ran stops at such a point, you ask and pass the answer on. Record the question and the answer you received in your final message.

A result whose `status` is `pending` is not an answer: no answer has come yet and the question stays open for the operator. Call `devflow_ask` again with the same arguments plus the `question_id` that result gave, and keep doing so until you receive an answer or a `devflow_ask closed:` result. On a result starting `devflow_ask refused:`, fix the payload and call again. On a result starting `devflow_ask closed:` (the run was stopped, aborted or timed out), end the stage and put that text in your final line's reason. If the call itself fails or the tool is not available, do not resolve the question yourself; report it instead.

## Completion Protocol (REQUIRED)

When all work is done, the LAST line of your FINAL message must be exactly:

DEVFLOW_RESULT: {"status": "success"}

If something prevents completion:

DEVFLOW_RESULT: {"status": "failed", "reason": "specific explanation"}

Anything else your final message must contain, such as the reasoning for a decision, goes above the DEVFLOW_RESULT line. DevFlow reads this line to decide whether the stage succeeded. Output nothing after it.
